<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Galigo</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sureq Galigo, I La Galigo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">La Galigo, or Sureq Galigo, is the epic cycle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bugis">Bugis</a> of South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, composed in Buginese verse and handed down in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a>. It tells of the descent of the gods to earth and the adventures of the hero Sawérigading and his son I La Galigo, many of them set in Luwu. Its manuscripts, mostly of the 18th and 19th centuries, form one of the longest literary works in the world and were added to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/memory-of-the-world-programme">Memory of the World Register</a> in 2011.</p></div>
